<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea says supplies 700 bln won to banks.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea says supplies 700 bln won to banks.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Korea said on Friday it supplied 700 billion won to commercial banks through three-day repurchase agreements to relieve the short-term liquidity shortage in the money market.  </p>
<p>&quot;We have decided to supply 700 billion won to help banks meet their reserve requirement obligations,&quot; said an official at the Bank of Korea.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
